{title: I Am Against You}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 38:1–3; 38:4–9; 38:10–16; 38:18–23; 39:1–12; Revelation 20:7–10}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Dm] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Son of man set your face against [Eb]Gog
[Bb]Chief prince of Mes[F]hech
The [Gm]word of the Lord came to [Eb]me
I am a[Bb]gainst you I de[F]clare
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [Gm]turn you around with a hook [Eb]
Bring you [Bb]out with your whole ar[F]my
Horses [Gm]and horsemen splendid[Eb]ly clothed
[Bb]A vast company with [F]shields
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]Persia and Cush and Put are [Eb]with them
[Bb]Gomer and Beth Togarmah from the [F]north
[Gm]Many peoples gathered around [Eb]you
Prepare [Bb]yourself for the bat[F]tle
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]In the latter years you will in[Eb]vade
A [Bb]land that has recovered from [F]war
Peo[Gm]ple gathered to the mountains of [Eb]Israel
[Bb]Living in safety and [F]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gm]You will come like [Eb]a storm on the land
[Bb]A cloud covering the [F]sky
[Gm]Thinking in your heart an e[Eb]vil scheme
To [Bb]plunder the unwalled villa[F]ges
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [Gm]turn you around with a hook [Eb]
Bring you [Bb]out with your whole ar[F]my
Horses and [Gm]horsemen splendidly [Eb]clothed
[Bb]A vast company with [F]shields
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]My hot anger [Eb]will flare up that day
[Bb]A great earthquake in the [F]land
[Gm]Mountains will be torn down [Eb]and fall
[Bb]The sword against his [F]brother
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm]I will pour down rain and [Eb]hailstones
[Bb]Fire and sulfur on [F]you
[Gm]Show my greatness and [Eb]my holiness
They will [Bb]know that I am the [F]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Seven months they [Eb]will bury the dead
[Bb]Cleansing the land for the [F]Lord
[Gm]Valley of Gog's [Eb]Horde it shall be
[Bb]Fire from heaven con[F]sumes [Gm]them
{end_of_verse}

